+
+### Reading a baseline
+
+The bytes of a baseline always come from `state/objects/`; apply makes no network call, and a
+missing baseline stops the apply before anything is written. Read a baseline with
+`node <package>/scripts/resolve-base.mjs --path <canonical path> --out <file>`. Exit 4 means the
+object is missing, so stop before writing anything. Exit 3 means
+the entry is a bundle, git or local snapshot, so read it from that source instead.
